# Fork (giantswarm/agentgateway-upstream): time-boxed acceptances of image-scan
# findings the line cannot fix itself (publish.yaml scans every own image; a
# FIXABLE HIGH/CRITICAL finding is never listed here — bump the dependency,
# upstream first). One finding per line, with an expiry and a reason; an expired
# entry fails the scan again and is re-triaged, never just extended:
#
#   CVE-2026-NNNNN exp:2026-12-31 # <package@version>: why no fix exists upstream, what to track, tracked in <owner>/<repo>#NN

# istio.io/istio is imported at a v0.0.0-<date> pseudo-version of a 2026 commit;
# Trivy cannot order a pseudo-version against the advisories' fixed releases
# (Istio <= 1.13) and flags advisories the code is years past. Re-triage when the
# controller pins an istio.io/istio release tag or Trivy learns pseudo-versions.
# Tracked in giantswarm/giantswarm#37758.
CVE-2019-14993 exp:2026-12-31 # istio.io/istio@v0.0.0-20260806113403-f1a56063393c: envoy regex DoS, fixed in Istio 1.1.13/1.2.4 — pseudo-version false positive
CVE-2021-39155 exp:2026-12-31 # istio.io/istio@v0.0.0-20260806113403-f1a56063393c: case-insensitive host authz bypass, fixed in Istio 1.9.8/1.10.4/1.11.1 — pseudo-version false positive
CVE-2021-39156 exp:2026-12-31 # istio.io/istio@v0.0.0-20260806113403-f1a56063393c: URI fragment authz bypass, fixed in Istio 1.9.8/1.10.4/1.11.1 — pseudo-version false positive
CVE-2022-23635 exp:2026-12-31 # istio.io/istio@v0.0.0-20260806113403-f1a56063393c: unauthenticated control-plane DoS, fixed in Istio 1.13.1/1.12.4/1.11.7 — pseudo-version false positive
